TITLE: [SRF-SP-ROW][CXL] Remote Core to CXL Bandwidth degrade of 5-20% observed across 100NTW, 1R1W, 2R1W, 1R1NTW, 2R1NTW WLs in PLR1/PLR2

DESCRIPTION:
Remote Core to CXL Bandwidth shows a degrade of 5-20% for W2,W5,W6, W7 and W8 KPIs as compared to Targets. Please refer to the Attachment - CXL_Remote_Final_HSD_v1.xlsx / 2_Tier-603_BKC97vsBKC98_Final, Core to CXL 2 Tier measurements. The measurements were done on both PLR1 and PLR2 and seeing similar degrades in both the Releases. System Name fl31ca103an0304.amr.corp.intel.com QDF RPG3 No of CXL Cards 4 (2 CXL cards each on Soc0 and Soc1) CXL Mode 2 Tier CXL Card Model Astera A0 CXL FW Version 1.3.0 FW Speed 5600 CXL DDR5 Size 64GB * 2 (1 DPC) Native DDR5 size 32GB * 8

COMMENTS:
As part of the debug, have tried the following steps. Exp 1 : Tried the affected Remote KPIs on 3 different setups to confirm issue consistency :     System Issue observed?  % of Delta  Comments fl31ca103bs0603 Yes 3-20% This system was received from NPI as part of CXL transition fl41ca202js0403 Partially (for 100NTW, 2R1NTW, 1R1NTW) 2-5% This is NPI system that was used to publish the numbers in the NPI report fl31ca103an0304 Yes 3-20% Brought up the new system with CXL hardware from 603 system above to rule out system/CXL card problem Outcome :- Same CXL hardware on the different system with same BIOS/OS/other hardware peripherals shows the same issue. CXL Hardware could be the issue. Exp2: On the new setup fl31ca103an0304 tried the below : Used 304 system from above Experiment row No.3 and replaced 4 CXL cards (S0 and S1) Re-flashing the CXL FW  Enabling maximum cooling for the system to avoid thermal throttling.   Outcome :- Still see 3-20% delta for all Workloads. This means with 2 systems and 2 different sets of CXL cards we are seeing the problem. Exp3: Check soc1 local core to CXL path      W2 S0  S1  NPI Score Local Core to CXL 147 135 142   Outcome :- Soc1 local core to CXL not able to match Soc0 core to CXL. Hence suspecting issue with soc1 core to cxl path or soc1 connected CXL cards. Exp4:  Compare S0 to S1 and S1 to S0 Remote Bandwidth.     W2 S0 to S1 S1 to S0 NPI Data Remote Core to CXL 83 83.7 90   Outcome :- From Exp3 local S1 bandwidth shortfall does not seem to be affecting S0 to S1 vs S1 to S0.
When we received the system from NPI, the CXL cards FW version was 1.1, upgraded it to 1.3. Just to cross check went back to FW version 1.1 and ran the same Remote KPI measurements. Please see below table for the measurements Observations: 1. For most Workloads(except 100%NTW sequential and random) we recover the bandwidth with FW version 1.1 (compare col. L vs R) 2. With FW version 1.1 vs 1.3 local CXL to mem we do not see any large deltas (Please see attachment) 3. Suspecting IIO path on socket 1 to cxl cards is causing bandwidth degrade, will collect EMON for PLR2 test CXL FW version 1.1 vs 1.3 as the next step.
@Thomas, Princy V Can you try suggestion from Ivan? Can you capture the temperature reading with FWv1.1 vs FWv1.3 to see on both local and remote with MLC? Note: Adding the comment for future refence from HSDES (attached email)   From: Cuevas Escareno, Ivan D    Sent: Wednesday, March 26, 2025 9:07 PM  To: Thomas, Princy V  Cc: Dambal, Prafulla ; Cs, Abhi ; Vyapron, Shaji Nittukkandy  Subject: RE: Need help with the HSD : https://hsdes.intel.com/appstore/article-one/#/article/14024625060    Hi Princy,   If you suspect issue is when moving Astera’s FW then it could be thermal throttling. Astera have been adjusting temperature thresholds in their releases and maybe you are exceeding that with 1.3 (95 degrees Celsius)   Can you please run leo_read_tsod_example while you run your mlc test and confirm if you are not exceeding the threshold? Binary is included in the SDK you use to upgrade your Astera’s FWs.   Thanks, Ivan
@Cs, Abhi ,   I have tried leo_read_tsod_example and the temperature seems to be well within 40 deg Celsius on all the CXL cards while running the mlc test.
The Core to CXL Remote bandwidth KPIs have been run on different Astera FW versions like FW1.2, 1.3 and 1.6. The issue seems to exist on all FW versions > FW1.1.  Emon data for all the versions has been collected and attached --> Emon_AllFW @Tu, Alan S,  Could you please update your findings on the EMON collected across different FWs?
After comparing results of different Astera FW versions were were able to isolate the drop to a change in FW1.2.0. This is only observed in SRF, not in GNR. After collecting emon of FW 1.1.0 and FW 1.2.0 we are not seeing any abnormal behavior in SOC. The current theory is that some change occured in FW 1.2.0 that is impacting internally to the CXL device, perhaps causing higher latency. There is no detail provided in the release notes that I am seeing. Consulting with Astera vendor experts for insights.
Some change seems to have been introduced in FW1.2 which is sensitive to the directory mode feature in SRF. Below table has the data for Directory mode @Auto vs Directory mode disabled on both FW1.1 and FW1.2. By disabling the directory mode, it is observed that some of the bandwidth recovers across these KPIs, however not all KPIs show an improvement. Also observe that the improvement is higher on FW1.1 when compared to FW1.2. This needs to be further investigated on why the Astera FW is showing this behavior with FW > 1.2 versions
@Ganesh, Akshar  - Can you check and ensure that this is not card issue? Do we have any other CXL card to validate this case? Once confirmed we will reach out to design team for further debug.
I verified the PnP CXL Configuration .  Astera card ,  Memory  Configuration , Firmware  Everything Looks proper .Card is Functional .
As per the discussion in standup meeting with Shaji, this needs to be pursued with Astera card FW changes in >= 1.2 particularly when used (but not limited to) in directory mode.  CXL Team to work with Astera team for further invistation of FW Version upgrades.
@Dixit, Shripad  - If we are pursuing the issue with the Astera, then we should reject the transferred sighting and continue with Astera folks. Could you reject the sighting central issue?
@Appaji, Sudhir - i would like to keep in sighting_central as there is a good traction there. Our current data is for Astera Vendor. Do we have data for other CXL Vendors like RPB and Montage ?
@Dixit, Shripad  -Vendor issues are not tracked through sighting central tenant, it is done from platf server tenant. So this cannot be an exception. Lets align offline. Please check with CXL owners on numbers with other CXL vendor card.
Sent below comparison data to Astera for feedback. They requested to test with latest FW V1.8.6 and latest HW stepping B0. Below results show that impact is to remote traffic in default SRF directory mode (enabled) starting in FW V1.2.0 We are in the process of updating to Astera B0 cards in the system and will add those data points as well. Local CXL Memory V1.1.0 V1.2.0 V1.8.6 V1.2.0 vs V1.1.0 V1.8.6 vs V1.1.0 DIR default DIR enabled DIR disabled DIR default DIR enabled DIR disabled DIR default DIR disabled DIR default DIR enabled DIR disabled DIR default DIR disabled R seq 106402.4 106435.7 106443.1 104791.3 104831.4 104828 104799.9 104831.2 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 R rand 106322.5 106369.4 106367.3 104718.8 104768.1 104743.9 104705 104722.6 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 W2 seq 148686.5 148687.3 148594.3 147429.2 147388.1 147309.2 148463.4 148178.7 0.99 0.99 0.99 1.00 1.00 W2 rand 142548.1 142184.8 142950.3 141099.9 141114.9 141840.2 141990 141929.6 0.99 0.99 0.99 1.00 0.99 W5 seq 146609.1 146635.8 146628.8 145502 145496.7 145435.6 146553.1 146582.1 0.99 0.99 0.99 1.00 1.00 W5 rand 140825.6 140564.7 140715.6 138892.6 138845.3 139089.3 140272.8 140820.6 0.99 0.99 0.99 1.00 1.00 W6 seq 90818.8 90847.3 90764.3 89357.5 89394.9 89418.3 89400.5 89490.7 0.98 0.98 0.99 0.98 0.99 W6 rand 90400.4 90376.3 90388.5 88964.1 88917.9 88998.1 88961.2 89002 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 0.98 W7 seq 137288.5 137117.4 135838.3 132300.6 132273.1 131097 134047 132829.4 0.96 0.96 0.97 0.98 0.98 W7 rand 131385.8 131430.7 130194.4 126752.5 126600.4 125414.5 128454.7 127234.1 0.96 0.96 0.96 0.98 0.98 W8 seq 135438.6 135275.3 133931.3 130719.1 130643.4 129751.6 131989.5 131368.3 0.97 0.97 0.97 0.97 0.98 W8 rand 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0           Idle latency seq 293.1 294.9 361.9 311.5 312.6 368.1 305.4 365.1 0.94 0.94 0.98 0.96 0.99 Idle latency rand 294.1 294.7 362.2 311.4 311.7 369 306.2 365 0.94 0.95 0.98 0.96 0.99   Remote CXL Memory V1.1.0 V1.2.0 V1.8.6 V1.2.0 vs V1.1.0 V1.8.6 vs V1.1.0 DIR default DIR enab