Hello @Schofield, Alison , have the changes landed upstream & BKC?
@Avelar, Omar  The patch is in upstream review and you can track it in https://jira.devtools.intel.com/browse/LINUXBKC3-132 I can tell you that it did not get merged in the 6.10 window, so next chance is the 6.11 merge. It's part of a set that does a bit more cleanup than this HSD needed, so if BKC folks do want to merge it they could select the first patch in the set only.
Here's an update on the patches upstream journey: It was accepted by an x86 maintainer and merged into the upstream 'tip' tree here: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tip/tip.git/commit/?h=x86/cpu&id=079544ec60fcba3f32e4b513442cc131211c8e22 It is queued for v6.11 kernel release.
@Avelar, Omar I have backport the fix patch and build a test kernel as follows, https://bee.sh.intel.com/~yhuang/bkc/kernel-6.6.0_06745_g53ff8c3466c6_dirty-2.x86_64.rpm can you help to give it a try?
@Huang, Ying  Did you get the right patch?  There were 2 in the set. This one does the actual work needed here: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tip/tip.git/commit/?h=x86/cpu&id=98b83cf0c1e22390ebfeb96b3c1b40f7189c558a
@Schofield, Alison Yes.  Actually I only backport this one and its dependency.
System can not boot to OS with below test kernel. https://bee.sh.intel.com/~yhuang/bkc/kernel-6.6.0_06745_g53ff8c3466c6_dirty-2.x86_64.rpm I am trying to re-build a test kernel with patch: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tip/tip.git/commit/?h=x86/cpu&id=98b83cf0c1e22390ebfeb96b3c1b40f7189c558a Will update when I get test result.
Test kernel is not reproducing the original issue.
Awaiting BKC integration. WIP - Release Notes 2024 WW28 GNR Fix kernel not being aware of TME AES-XTS-256 (HSD 14018115093)
staged as  srf-6.6-v25.6
Tested to behave as per https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tip/tip.git/commit/?h=x86/cpu&id=98b83cf0c1e22390ebfeb96b3c1b40f7189c558a. Moving to complete.

TITLE: [GNR SP VV][BKC][2024WW52][X2][8S][Stability]vmap allocation for size 188416 failed during cycling

DESCRIPTION:
