@Pan, Lijun , any update from kernel side? Any further debugging action needs to be taken?
I will revert one of the potential regression patch and get back to you when the rpms are generated.
@Pan, Lijun Sure, BTW the changes is inside the kernel or just some packages' changes, which patch do you suspect?
I reverted this patch which may relate to the issue, please have a try this one. code: https://github.com/intel-innersource/os.linux.kernel.bkc/commits/test/15017291534-v1 rpm: http://linuxbkc-devops.jf.intel.com/kernel-builds/bkc-6.6/250115/9978cf3f976f/
