In today's meeting with  @Shulzhenko, Oleksandr and  @Spica, Michal , we discussed this issue and agree to demote it to p4. In summary,  this issue is more likely to be an environment issue. when we first hit the issue, we modified our script to poll the temperature, which used many peci commands. As 1862284465 said, many peci commands might cause this issue. Then for the debugging of the issue, we ran the rss.sh from bmc and wrongly stored the log inside the bmc. This wrong debug behavior also led to the oom kernel panic and we saw pretty high failure rate ~1/200. The systems which reproduced this issue during ww06-ww07 's bmc room space might also be full. We first hit the issue 2x in 500 cycles on two systems. When we flashed the EB, the space of bmc was cleaned and there was no reproduction. That is the most likely reason why we did not reproduce after EB flashing.  Now we flashed the formal bkc version bmc 24.51 and rerun the test on these two systems, there is also no reproduction for around 500 cycles. From the issue behavior, it is more like rss.sh's log polluted the environment, so demote the HSD to p4 and monitor it for one more week
